  "mechanismSummary": "2-Bromo-2-methylbutane has β-hydrogens on two CH₃ groups and on one CH₂. Ethoxide would give mainly the more substituted 2-methylbut-2-ene. tert-Butoxide is bulky: it reaches the exposed CH₃ hydrogens more easily than the hindered CH₂ ones, so the less substituted 2-methylbut-1-ene is the main product (about 70%), the Hofmann product.",
